# Citation metadata for IMPD-CS (Citation File Format 1.2.0; GitHub shows it as "Cite this repository").
# Zenodo archives each GitHub release. `doi` is the concept DOI, which covers all versions and resolves to the
# latest release; the DOI of each released version is listed under `identifiers` (added after its release).
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use IMPD-CS, cite it with its version and build identity (docs/BUILD_ID), and cite the DANS deposits
  of the surveys you use (README.md, "Citing the sources").
type: software
title: "IMPD-CS: harmonized cross-sections of Dutch migrant surveys, 2002-2020 (code, crosswalks and codebook)"
abstract: >-
  IMPD-CS is the cross-sectional component of the Integrated Migrant Panel Dataset. It harmonizes the DANS deposits
  of eight Dutch surveys of persons with a migration background (SPVA 2002, SPVN 2003, LAS 2004/05, SIM 2006,
  SING 2009, SIM 2011, SIM 2015, SIM 2020) into one person-level file of repeated cross-sections, with English
  theme-stemmed variable names, shared value sets and one missing-value scheme, reproducible in R and in Stata
  from the deposits and a set of CSV crosswalks. The repository holds the code, the crosswalks and the generated
  codebook; the data are rebuilt by each user from the DANS deposits.
